WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.890
The Digital World,

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:06.070
a world inhabited by unusual 
creatures called Digimon.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:09.950
It has been conquered 
by the evil Bagra Army

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.510
and divided into seven Kingdoms 
ruled by seven Death Generals.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.260
Taiki Kudou has leapt 
into these seven Kingdoms

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.060
along with his partner, 
Shoutmon, to save the Digimon.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.700
This is the story of the 
friendship and adventures

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.540
shared by Taiki, his friends, 
and the Digimon.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:53.880
Our battle with the 
enemy emperor, Bagramon,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.390
has finally begun at 
the Great Bagra Palace.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:58.890
But Bagramon's strength was too immense,

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.500
and his plan to destroy everything, 
including the human world,

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.270
D5, began right before our eyes.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.450
I was thrown underground to the 
Great Bagra Palace's depths.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.410
There we found a mysterious place

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.640
where we thought Yuu might be, 
so we busted in.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.080
Meanwhile, Kiriha and Nene 
continued to fight with all they had,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.020
but during the battle...

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.400
But have you forgotten?

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.510
For what purpose do you think 
I discovered the DigiXros?

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.960
Darkness Loader DigiXros!

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.130
No! Stop this!

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:53.230
<b>Drawing Nigh!</b>

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:53.230
<b>The End of the Human World, D5!!</b>

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.470
Drawing Nigh!

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.690
The End of the Human World, D5!!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.860
I knew you'd be here, Yuu!

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.840
What power!

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:06.830
So this is my brother's power?

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.750
It's overwhelming!

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.540
There's no way I could have won!

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:16.490
But now, it belongs to me.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.760
My brother has become a part of 
me through a forced DigiXros.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.220
Everything is going as I expected.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.190
That's what you were hoping for?

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.190
That's right, Nene.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:33.150
My brother, Bagramon, 
with his superdimensional power,

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.650
was in a class of his own.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:39.960
I trained desperately to be 
able to triumph over him.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.510
But the stronger I grew,

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.840
the more I felt the difference 
in our abilities.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.210
My brother always accepted me generously,

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:51.650
even knowing my competitive nature.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:56.200
I simply could not bear that.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.610
That is why I invented the Xros Loader,

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.890
and searched for a human who 
could enable a powerful DigiXros

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.660
so that my brother would be impressed.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.390
And the one I found...

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.930
was Yuu.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:17.540
And for that... just for that, 
you played with our destinies?

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.410
That's right.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.440
And as a result, 
my wish finally came true.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:27.540
There is no Digimon left in this 
world who matches my worth!

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.720
What do we do, Kiriha?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:34.990
There's nothing we can do!

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:35.930
Let's run for now!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.700
I will wipe out your very souls.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.990
God of Death Snatcher!

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.100
If that thing touches you, you're dead!

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:51.500
An attack that destroys 
Digimon, down to their data?

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.380
What is this feeling?

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:02.330
Some sort of terrible Digital 
crisis has occurred.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.620
If we don't hurry back, 
Kiriha and Nene are in danger.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.650
Let's get Yuu out of here, quick!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.380
What are you? Out of the way!

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.660
He... Digivolved?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:22.680
No, he was compressing his 
own data to become smaller.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.880
He's most likely guarding Yuu.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.340
Be careful! He is powerful!

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.990
Xros Heart?

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:50.280
Taiki! Taiki's alive!

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:52.600
Yuu!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.540
It's no use! 
We have to find his weakness!

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.870
A mouse Digimon's weakness...

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.980
Reload, Bastemon!

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.200
Did you need something, Master Taiki?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.390
My, what a racket.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.580
Look at the enemy Digimon.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:16.650
I'm scared!

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.510
How strange.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.580
When I look at that Digimon,

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.190
I suddenly feel...

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:27.000
...like quite the savage beast!

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.500
How crude.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.320
Absolutely unsightly.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:39.270
What do you gain from surviving 
when you cannot win,

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:40.780
Kiriha? Nene?

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.750
If we don't survive, we can't fight back!

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.950
Yeah! No matter what 
happens, we won't give up!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:51.350
With no game pieces left to 
fight, it won't be that easy.

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:53.730
Darkness Loader DigiXros!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.140
I've already won.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.910
You have no more need for Xros Loaders.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:05.350
I'll make them part of me, along 
with the Digimon inside them.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.680
You should feel honored.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.140
What?!

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:11.210
He's pulling us to him!

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.870
This is very bad!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.610
Very bad!

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:15.950
Nene, do something!

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.800
What a great feeling!

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:23.620
So this is how it feels to 
stand on the top as ruler!

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.670
It is extraordinary, Brother!

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.400
Ah, I feel so much better.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.820
Thanks, Bastemon.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:44.040
I see. A mouse's weakness is a cat.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.740
No... I feel as if I've just seen 
a side of the Princess

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.380
I should never have seen...

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.250
Scary...

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.520
Yuu! Hang in there, Yuu!

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.920
Taiki...

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.690
But how? I thought you were dead.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:05.100
Oh, you mean how we 
escaped from Hell's Field?

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:09.590
We forced the game to 
end using death data.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.010
To save both you and me.

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:15.910
I see.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.270
Thank goodness you're okay.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.680
But Damemon...

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.450
Damemon is gone, because of me.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.190
And not just Damemon.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.880
My playing around took the 
lives of so many Digimon.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:35.090
That was the one thing 
I hated the most...

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.630
Yet I did the exact same things

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:40.200
from the moment I came 
to the Digital World.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.920
I'm the worst!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.440
That's not true, Yuu.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:48.410
As if a superman like you 
could understand how I feel!

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.740
Of course I do.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:53.080
I'm no superman. I'm just like you.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.710
And I can't turn my back on you.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.150
Why?

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:58.010
Why can't you?

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.290
If it were me, I could 
never go and save you!

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:02.920
Why?

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.290
What do you mean, why?

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.790
See? We are different!

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:10.300
You're using the logic 
of a strong person!

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:11.950
But I... I...

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:14.430
Oh, shut up already, you brat!

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:18.760
Hey, Mervamon!

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:22.410
I just put him to sleep. 
We're in enough danger as it is.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.320
She's right. We must hurry 
and blow up this place.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:29.380
Of course, it'd be best to 
do so after we've escaped.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.260
You're right. Revolmon!

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.080
Okay, leave it to me!

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:38.790
Why can't I turn my back on you, huh?

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.390
I can't take it anymore!

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.230
So this is the end for 
my long-time enemies.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.510
Though, I already have ultimate strength.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.470
You will only make me slightly stronger.

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:55.130
In some ways, a goal is 
such a transient thing.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.410
The special tower where Yuu is being kept!

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:03.280
What's going on?

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.750
It can't be!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.380
Yes, it can!

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:07.420
Taiki!

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:10.650
We've blown up that facility of yours!

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.120
And we've rescued Yuu!

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:13.220
Yuu!

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.830
Yuu... Yuu!

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.400
Sis...

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.290
You finally got him back, Nene.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.940
Sticking with you was worthwhile.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.680
Yeah. Thank you, Mervamon.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:37.180
You're a guy who doesn't 
go down without a fight.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:39.310
I could say the same for you.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:40.790
Great job sticking it out.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:46.020
So I can't draw the power to 
DigiXros out of Yuu anymore?

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:48.660
But that makes no difference now!

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:58.690
I will make it all happen 
with nothing but this body.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:03.680
I'll carry out the plan to merge the 
Digital and human worlds through D5,

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.680
and make everything mine!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:11.720
That will be my memorial for my 
brother, who lives within me now.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:14.900
He absorbed Bagramon?

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.090
Yes. He's out of our league now.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:18.760
What can we do?

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.930
At this rate, both worlds will 
belong to DarkKnightmon!

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:24.730
The Dark Stone.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:27.080
We don't have to defeat him.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.110
If we can just stop the Dark Stone 
in his chest from functioning,

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:32.220
we can at least stop D5.

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:34.140
That's where we'll start.

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:35.290
Sounds good.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.020
Even if the situation is hopeless,

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:40.100
it's worth trying if there's 
a goal to work toward.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.050
Let's try it. Is everyone okay?

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:44.880
I wouldn't say that, but...

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.200
This isn't the time to talk like that!

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.670
We have no choice!

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.360
We'll fight, Nene!

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.470
All right, let's go!

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.590
Great Xros!

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:56.690
Shoutmon!

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:58.800
MetalGreymon!

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.930
Digivolve!

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:02.760
OmegaShoutmon!

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.140
ZekeGreymon!

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.670
Ballistamon!

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.040
Dorulumon!

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:11.740
Starmons!

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.120
Yes!

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:14.970
Sparrowmon!

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.430
Great Xros!

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.890
Shoutmon X7!

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:25.760
Fools!

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.500
This time I'll reduce you to nothing!

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:29.490
God of Death Snatcher!

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:33.550
Taiki, if that hits them, their data 
will be chipped away to nothing!

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.750
Shoutmon X7!

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:40.000
Xros Burning Rocker!

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>Original Digimon Contest! The Five Special Award Winners</b>

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>4. The General Arashi Award</b>

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>Kenta's Design</b>

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>Ganemon</b>

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.520
Resistance is futile!

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:54.490
We won't know that until we try!

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:57.490
Besides, you're not 
as strong as Bagramon!

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:59.620
What nonsense is this?!

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.460
His power dropped!

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:05.130
Now, Starmons!

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:09.270
Okay! We won't lose this big chance!

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:12.940
Seven Victorize!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.870
Does this mean I'm weaker 
than my brother alone?

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:22.650
Don't be ridiculous! 
I should have surpassed him!

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.620
I should have surpassed my brother!

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.750
Th-This pulse... Is it my brother's?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:37.160
That is enough, little brother.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:40.850
Brother!

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:45.700
You still couldn't defeat me in the end.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:51.030
But... Then, you knew of my plan?

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.000
Of course I did.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.860
I knew what you were 
doing behind my back,

00:13:54.860 --> 00:14:00.690
and how desperately you endorsed D5, 
which would give you an opening.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.020
I saw through it all.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:06.120
Then why did you throw it away?

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:10.930
I also knew that it was 
not likely to work.

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:12.500
What?!

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:20.590
So your strength exceeded 
mine to the very end...

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:22.540
Until now!

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:25.650
My dear little brother,

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:29.970
my pitiful little brother who has 
lived under the name of nobility

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.370
all this time, just to 
make himself look good.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:34.600
I will tell you in your final moments...

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.210
What you lack is ideals,

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.890
and the conviction to support them.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:42.130
Ideals and conviction...

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:46.630
That was the gap between 
us that I could never fill.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:49.570
I had high hopes for you, 
but I was disappointed.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:52.520
Disappear behind that visage...

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.210
while still inside me.

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.110
No... No!

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:57.710
Not after I've come this far!

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:09.500
What happened? He stopped moving.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.060
What happened to DarkKnightmon?

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:13.420
He is dead.

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:14.170
What?

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:48.990
This is the true form 
of DarknessBagramon!

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:50.860
DarknessBagramon?

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:53.800
DarkKnightmon's been absorbed himself!

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:58.570
Yes. He did not have the disposition 
to become a true king.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:02.410
Gimme a break! 
And you're saying you do?!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.960
Naturally.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.150
I have ideals and conviction.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:11.690
The ideal of merging the 
Digital and human worlds,

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:15.280
and the strong conviction 
needed to accomplish it.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.570
You think I'm gonna let you do that?!

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:24.650
This is the ultimate power 
that my brother sought.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:37.540
Shoutmon!

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.550
You disgust me. Disappear.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:42.590
If you want to erase me, 
go ahead and try.

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:44.580
I won't give up.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:49.250
Humans... Taiki and the others... 
gave us incredible power.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:52.990
Why does that have to be destroyed?

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:56.030
Humans are incomplete beings.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:17:00.040
My power is needed to recreate them,

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:04.910
and to make the Digital World 
even greater at the same time.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.000
You can't...

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:12.020
See? I knew it.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.630
You're no king!

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.910
What?!

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:19.180
I realized it through all the battles 
we've fought to get this far.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:23.500
A true king is someone who 
believes in everyone else.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.710
Everyone is waiting for someone

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.510
who believes that they can 
become strong someday!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:32.620
Someone like you who doesn't 
believe in his partner's potential

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:34.100
has no right to be a king!

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:35.630
But don't worry.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:38.940
I will become the Digimon King!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.770
I see.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:46.380
You have far greater ideals and 
conviction than my brother did.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:49.190
I am moved, Shoutmon.

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:52.620
Then just try to stop me.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.270
Shoutmon!

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:04.970
Shoutmon! Shoutmon!

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:08.620
Don't cry, Taiki. 
The fight's not over yet.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:10.900
Idiot! Don't try to talk!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.710
I have to crush the Dark Stone, right?

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:16.210
I leave the rest to you.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:19.240
Okay... I'll see you around!

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:46.490
Shoutmon!

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.710
Taiki...

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:57.270
<i>I'm no superman. I'm just like you.</i>

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.200
You...

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.850
I won't forgive you for that, 
DarknessBagramon!

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:05.620
Burning with rage won't do you any good.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:09.230
Now, I shall descend upon the human world!

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:16.770
All of you will disappear

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:20.560
to the eternal realm 
between time and space,

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.850
in neither the Digital 
nor the human world!

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:28.400
You will never see the new 
world I am about to create!

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:32.300
Eternal Darkmare!

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:42.800
Time to go.

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.410
Imperfect human world,

00:19:55.880 --> 00:20:00.750
be reborn by my hand!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:09.720
Shoutmon... everyone...

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:13.590
It's no use. I can't hear their voices.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:17.260
I couldn't do anything... nothing...

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:19.490
Even though Shoutmon trusted me

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:22.420
and mustered up the last of his strength...

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:27.450
He was the first Digimon I met, 
and my best friend...

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.440
Is this the end?

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:33.540
<i>Don't cry, Taiki. 
The fight's not over yet.</i>

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.020
That's right. I'm not finished yet!

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.730
I can't be finished!

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:43.690
Found him!

00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:45.690
One, two!

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.960
It's unusual to see you crying.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:50.890
But you can't give up yet, Taiki.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:55.430
Because the friends you can trust, 
more than anyone else, are back!

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:59.780
Zenjirou! Akari!

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.890
Shoutmon and the others are...

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:04.300
Looks like some kind of miracle happened.

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:05.740
Guys!

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:08.620
Akari and Zenjirou saved us,

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.720
by calling out to us 
through the darkness.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:13.190
I'm so happy to see you again!

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.550
Cutemon!

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.710
Thank you both.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.530
But Shoutmon is...

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:21.330
Taiki...

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:23.520
We heard from Nene and Kiriha.

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:25.360
But there's still hope!

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:29.730
There's still a way to rescue Shoutmon 
and save the human world!

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:32.100
H-How?

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:35.000
We will explain that.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:41.960
DigiMemories? Why do you have those?

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:45.180
These DigiMemories gave 
us the power to come here.

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:51.660
I am Examon.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:58.200
I am WarGreymon.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.500
Examon... WarGreymon...

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:04.340
Now, you children who 
call forth miracles,

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:07.710
we entrust our last hope to you.

00:22:07.710 --> 00:22:09.760
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:13.280
<b>Digimon Data Collection</b>

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:13.280
Digimon Data Collection!

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:17.210
<b>Listen to the Digimon's melody!</b>

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:17.210
Listen to the melody of 
this Digimon I caught!

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:15.230
<b>Melody starts in 3 seconds.</b>

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:16.230
<b>Melody starts in 2 seconds.</b>

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:17.210
<b>Melody starts in 1 second.</b>

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:32.660
<b>[Type]</b>

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:39.640
<b>Reptile Type</b>

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:32.660
<b>[Attacks]</b>

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:39.640
<b>Head Strike  
Kilo Flame</b>

00:22:27.190 --> 00:22:28.920
Gaossmon.

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:32.830
His attack is a powerful 
headbutt, Head Strike.

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:36.060
He has a really hard head!

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:39.640
Then I bet he's not very good at riddles!

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:44.040
There's only one way to save Shoutmon.

00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:45.720
No matter how dangerous it is...

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:47.210
Go, Taiki!

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:48.450
The future depends on you!

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:50.450
Thanks, everyone!

00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:52.520
Digimon Xros Wars!

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.470
<b>DigiXros of Glory,</b>

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.470
<b>Take Hold of Our Future!!</b>

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.520
You can't turn your back 
on the next one, either!
